<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Paduspanid dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">665 CE – 1598 CE (approx.) · capital Nur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A dynasty of mountain princes in Ruyan and Rustamdar that lasted over nine centuries, from the fall of the Sasanians to the reign of Shah Abbas.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-isfandiyar">Ibn Isfandiyar</a>, Paduspan, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gil-gavbara">Gil Gavbara</a> and brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dabuya">Dabuya</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dabuyid-dynasty">Dabuyid dynasty</a>, received the mountain region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruyan">Ruyan</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a> around 665. His descendants ruled this upland between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilan">Gilan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amol">Amol</a> as hereditary ostandars.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Paduspanids survived by submitting in turn to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/alavid-dynasty">Alavid dynasty</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/buyid-dynasty">Buyids</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a>, while keeping local power in fortresses such as Nur and Kojur. They converted from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zoroastrianism">Zoroastrianism</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and later to Shia Islam. In 1453 the dynasty split into two branches, at Nur and at Kojur, which often quarrelled. The region's economy rested on forests, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> and livestock.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran">Mazandaran</a> and its principalities in the 1590s, deposing the last Paduspanid rulers by 1598 and ending their rule.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 665 CE – 1598 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:72.94%;width:18.57%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>665 CE – 1598 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kayumars ibn Bisutun, Malik Jahangir</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Zoroastrianism, later Shia Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tabari, Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Paduspanids, Baduspanids</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1132&amp;focus=paduspanid-dynasty" aria-label="Paduspanid dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5987 859 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Paduspanid dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6307 1115L6281 1235"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6281 1235h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6307 1115h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6307 1115h0"/></svg><